---@field StorageLocation? aws.gamelift.S3Location Information indicating where your game build files are stored. Use this parameter only when creating a build with files stored in an Amazon S3 bucket that you own. The storage location must specify an Amazon S3 bucket name and key. The location must also specify a role ARN that you set up to allow Amazon GameLift Servers to access your Amazon S3 bucket. The S3 bucket and your new build must be in ...
---@field OperatingSystem? aws.gamelift.OperatingSystem|string The operating system that your game server binaries run on. This value determines the type of fleet resources that you use for this build. If your game build contains multiple executables, they all must run on the same operating system. You must specify a valid operating system in this request. There is no default value. You can't change a build's operating system later.
---@field Tags? aws.gamelift.TagList A list of labels to assign to the new build resource. Tags are developer defined key-value pairs. Tagging Amazon Web Services resources is useful for resource management, access management and cost allocation. For more information, see Tagging Amazon Web Services Resources in the Amazon Web Services General Reference. Once the resource is created, you can use TagResource, UntagResource, and ListTa...
---@field ServerSdkVersion? aws.gamelift.ServerSdkVersion A server SDK version you used when integrating your game server build with Amazon GameLift Servers. For more information see Integrate games with custom game servers. By default Amazon GameLift Servers sets this value to 4.0.2.

