---Set of rules for processing a deployment for a container fleet update. For how Amazon GameLift Servers validates and rolls out a deployment, see Container fleet deployments.
---@class aws.gamelift.DeploymentConfiguration
---@field ProtectionStrategy? aws.gamelift.DeploymentProtectionStrategy|string Determines how fleet deployment activity affects active game sessions on the fleet. A protected game session can't be terminated while it's active; a fleet sets the default protection for its new game sessions with NewGameSessionProtectionPolicy.
---@field MinimumHealthyPercentage? aws.gamelift.MinimumHealthyPercentage Sets the minimum percentage of the fleet's game server container groups to keep healthy during deployment activity. A low value favors deployment speed; a high value favors game server availability. For example, if the fleet runs 20 game server container groups and this value is 75, Amazon GameLift Servers keeps at least 15 of them healthy, so it replaces no more than 5 at a time.
---@field ImpairmentStrategy? aws.gamelift.DeploymentImpairmentStrategy|string Determines what actions to take if a deployment fails validation. If the fleet is multi-location, this strategy applies across all fleet locations.

---Information about the most recent deployment for the container fleet.
---@class aws.gamelift.DeploymentDetails
---@field LatestDeploymentId? aws.gamelift.DeploymentId A unique identifier for a fleet deployment.

---@alias aws.gamelift.DeploymentId string

---@alias aws.gamelift.DeploymentImpairmentStrategy "MAINTAIN"|"ROLLBACK"

---@alias aws.gamelift.DeploymentProtectionStrategy "WITH_PROTECTION"|"IGNORE_PROTECTION"

---@alias aws.gamelift.DeploymentStatus "IN_PROGRESS"|"IMPAIRED"|"COMPLETE"|"ROLLBACK_IN_PROGRESS"|"ROLLBACK_COMPLETE"|"CANCELLED"|"PENDING"

