---Log entry describing an event that involves Amazon GameLift Servers resources (such as a fleet). In addition to tracking activity, event codes and messages can provide additional information for troubleshooting and debugging problems.
---@class aws.gamelift.Event
---@field EventId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for a fleet event.
---@field ResourceId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for an event resource, such as a fleet ID.
---@field EventCode? aws.gamelift.EventCode The type of event being logged.
---@field Message? aws.gamelift.NonEmptyString Additional information related to the event.
---@field EventTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp Time stamp indicating when this event occurred. Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").
---@field PreSignedLogUrl? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString Location of stored logs with additional detail that is related to the event. This is useful for debugging issues. The URL is valid for 15 minutes. You can also access fleet creation logs through the Amazon GameLift Servers console.
---@field Count? aws.gamelift.EventCount The number of times that this event occurred.

---@alias aws.gamelift.EventCode "GENERIC_EVENT"|"FLEET_CREATED"|"FLEET_DELETED"|"FLEET_EXPIRED"|"FLEET_SCALING_EVENT"|"FLEET_STATE_DOWNLOADING"|"FLEET_STATE_VALIDATING"|"FLEET_STATE_BUILDING"|"FLEET_STATE_ACTIVATING"|"FLEET_STATE_ACTIVE"|"FLEET_STATE_ERROR"|"FLEET_STATE_PENDING"|"FLEET_STATE_CREATING"|"FLEET_STATE_CREATED"|"FLEET_STATE_UPDATING"|"FLEET_INITIALIZATION_FAILED"|"FLEET_BINARY_DOWNLOAD_FAILED"|"FLEET_VALIDATION_LAUNCH_PATH_NOT_FOUND"|"FLEET_VALIDATION_EXECUTABLE_RUNTIME_FAILURE"|"FLEET_VALIDATION_TIMED_OUT"|"FLEET_ACTIVATION_FAILED"|"FLEET_ACTIVATION_FAILED_NO_INSTANCES"|"FLEET_NEW_GAME_SESSION_PROTECTION_POLICY_UPDATED"|"SERVER_PROCESS_INVALID_PATH"|"SERVER_PROCESS_SDK_INITIALIZATION_TIMEOUT"|"SERVER_PROCESS_PROCESS_READY_TIMEOUT"|"SERVER_PROCESS_CRASHED"|"SERVER_PROCESS_TERMINATED_UNHEALTHY"|"SERVER_PROCESS_FORCE_TERMINATED"|"SERVER_PROCESS_PROCESS_EXIT_TIMEOUT"|"SERVER_PROCESS_SDK_INITIALIZATION_FAILED"|"SERVER_PROCESS_MISCONFIGURED_CONTAINER_PORT"|"GAME_SESSION_ACTIVATION_TIMEOUT"|"FLEET_CREATION_EXTRACTING_BUILD"|"FLEET_CREATION_RUNNING_INSTALLER"|"FLEET_CREATION_VALIDATING_RUNTIME_CONFIG"|"FLEET_VPC_PEERING_SUCCEEDED"|"FLEET_VPC_PEERING_FAILED"|"FLEET_VPC_PEERING_DELETED"|"INSTANCE_INTERRUPTED"|"INSTANCE_RECYCLED"|"INSTANCE_REPLACED_UNHEALTHY"|"FLEET_CREATION_COMPLETED_INSTALLER"|"FLEET_CREATION_FAILED_INSTALLER"|"COMPUTE_LOG_UPLOAD_FAILED"|"GAME_SERVER_CONTAINER_GROUP_CRASHED"|"PER_INSTANCE_CONTAINER_GROUP_CRASHED"|"GAME_SERVER_CONTAINER_GROUP_REPLACED_UNHEALTHY"|"LOCATION_STATE_PENDING"|"LOCATION_STATE_CREATING"|"LOCATION_STATE_CREATED"|"LOCATION_STATE_ACTIVATING"|"LOCATION_STATE_ACTIVE"|"LOCATION_STATE_UPDATING"|"LOCATION_STATE_ERROR"|"LOCATION_STATE_DELETING"|"LOCATION_STATE_DELETED"

---@alias aws.gamelift.EventCount number

---@alias aws.gamelift.EventList aws.gamelift.Event[]

---A list of fleet locations where a game session queue can place new game sessions. You can use a filter to temporarily exclude specific locations from receiving placements. For queues that have multi-location fleets, you can use a filter configuration to allow placement with some, but not all, of a fleet's locations.
---@class aws.gamelift.FilterConfiguration
---@field AllowedLocations? aws.gamelift.LocationList A list of locations to allow game session placement in, in the form of Amazon Web Services Region codes such as us-west-2.

---@alias aws.gamelift.FilterInstanceStatus "ACTIVE"|"DRAINING"

---@alias aws.gamelift.FilterInstanceStatuses (aws.gamelift.FilterInstanceStatus|string)[]

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetAction "AUTO_SCALING"

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetActionList (aws.gamelift.FleetAction|string)[]

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetArn string

---Describes an Amazon GameLift Servers fleet of game hosting resources. Attributes differ based on the fleet's compute type, as follows:
---@class aws.gamelift.FleetAttributes
---@field FleetId? aws.gamelift.FleetId A unique identifier for the fleet.
---@field FleetArn? aws.gamelift.FleetArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is assigned to a Amazon GameLift Servers fleet resource and uniquely identifies it. ARNs are unique across all Regions. Format is arn:aws:gamelift:::fleet/fleet-a1234567-b8c9-0d1e-2fa3-b45c6d7e8912. In a GameLift fleet ARN, the resource ID matches the FleetId value.
---@field FleetType? aws.gamelift.FleetType Indicates whether the fleet uses On-Demand or Spot instances. For more information, see On-Demand versus Spot Instances. This fleet property can't be changed after the fleet is created.
---@field InstanceType? aws.gamelift.EC2InstanceType The Amazon EC2 instance type that the fleet uses. Instance type determines the computing resources of each instance in the fleet, including CPU, memory, storage, and networking capacity. See Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud Instance Types for detailed descriptions. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is EC2.
---@field Description? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A human-readable description of the fleet.
---@field Name? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A descriptive label that is associated with a fleet. Fleet names do not need to be unique.
---@field CreationTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp A time stamp indicating when this data object was created. Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").
---@field TerminationTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp A time stamp indicating when this data object was terminated. Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").
---@field Status? aws.gamelift.FleetStatus Current status of the fleet. Possible fleet statuses include the following:
---@field BuildId? aws.gamelift.BuildId A unique identifier for the build resource that is deployed on instances in this fleet. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is "EC2".
---@field BuildArn? aws.gamelift.BuildArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) associated with the Amazon GameLift Servers build resource that is deployed on instances in this fleet. In a GameLift build ARN, the resource ID matches the BuildId value. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is "EC2".
---@field ScriptId? aws.gamelift.ScriptId A unique identifier for the Realtime script resource that is deployed on instances in this fleet. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is "EC2".
---@field ScriptArn? aws.gamelift.ScriptArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) associated with the GameLift script resource that is deployed on instances in this fleet. In a GameLift script ARN, the resource ID matches the ScriptId value.
---@field ServerLaunchPath? aws.gamelift.LaunchPathStringModel This parameter is no longer used. Server launch paths are now defined using the fleet's RuntimeConfiguration. Requests that use this parameter continue to be valid.
---@field ServerLaunchParameters? aws.gamelift.LaunchParametersStringModel This parameter is no longer used. Server launch parameters are now defined using the fleet's runtime configuration. Requests that use this parameter continue to be valid.
---@field LogPaths? aws.gamelift.StringList This parameter is no longer used. Game session log paths are now defined using the Amazon GameLift Servers server API ProcessReady() logParameters. See more information in the Server API Reference.
---@field NewGameSessionProtectionPolicy? aws.gamelift.ProtectionPolicy The type of game session protection to set on all new instances that are started in the fleet. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is EC2.
---@field OperatingSystem? aws.gamelift.OperatingSystem The operating system of the fleet's computing resources. A fleet's operating system is determined by the OS of the build or script that is deployed on this fleet. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is EC2.
---@field ResourceCreationLimitPolicy? aws.gamelift.ResourceCreationLimitPolicy
---@field MetricGroups? aws.gamelift.MetricGroupList Name of a metric group that metrics for this fleet are added to. In Amazon CloudWatch, you can view aggregated metrics for fleets that are in a metric group. A fleet can be included in only one metric group at a time. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is EC2.
---@field StoppedActions? aws.gamelift.FleetActionList A list of fleet activity that has been suspended using StopFleetActions. This includes fleet auto-scaling. This attribute is used with fleets where ComputeType is EC2.
---@field InstanceRoleArn? aws.gamelift.NonEmptyString A unique identifier for an IAM role that manages access to your Amazon Web Services services. With an instance role ARN set, any application that runs on an instance in this fleet can assume the role, including install scripts, server processes, and daemons (background processes). Create a role or look up a role's ARN by using the IAM dashboard in the Amazon Web Services Management Console. Learn ...
---@field CertificateConfiguration? aws.gamelift.CertificateConfiguration Determines whether a TLS/SSL certificate is generated for a fleet. This feature must be enabled when creating the fleet. All instances in a fleet share the same certificate.
---@field ComputeType? aws.gamelift.ComputeType The type of compute resource used to host your game servers. You can use your own compute resources with Amazon GameLift Servers Anywhere or use Amazon EC2 instances with managed Amazon GameLift Servers.
---@field AnywhereConfiguration? aws.gamelift.AnywhereConfiguration A set of attributes that are specific to an Anywhere fleet.
---@field InstanceRoleCredentialsProvider? aws.gamelift.InstanceRoleCredentialsProvider Indicates that fleet instances maintain a shared credentials file for the IAM role defined in InstanceRoleArn. Shared credentials allow applications that are deployed with the game server executable to communicate with other Amazon Web Services resources. This property is used only when the game server is integrated with the server SDK version 5.x. For more information about using shared credentia...
---@field PlayerGatewayMode? aws.gamelift.PlayerGatewayMode Indicates whether player gateway is enabled for this fleet. Player gateway provides benefits such as DDoS protection with negligible impact to latency.
---@field PlayerGatewayConfiguration? aws.gamelift.PlayerGatewayConfiguration Configuration settings for player gateway on this fleet.

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetAttributesList aws.gamelift.FleetAttributes[]

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetBinaryArn string

---Current resource capacity settings for managed EC2 fleets and managed container fleets. For multi-location fleets, location values might refer to a fleet's remote location or its home Region.
---@class aws.gamelift.FleetCapacity
---@field FleetId? aws.gamelift.FleetId A unique identifier for the fleet associated with the location.
---@field FleetArn? aws.gamelift.FleetArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is assigned to a Amazon GameLift Servers fleet resource and uniquely identifies it. ARNs are unique across all Regions. Format is arn:aws:gamelift:::fleet/fleet-a1234567-b8c9-0d1e-2fa3-b45c6d7e8912.
---@field InstanceType? aws.gamelift.EC2InstanceType The Amazon EC2 instance type that is used for instances in a fleet. Instance type determines the computing resources in use, including CPU, memory, storage, and networking capacity. See Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud Instance Types for detailed descriptions.
---@field InstanceCounts? aws.gamelift.EC2InstanceCounts The current number of instances in the fleet, listed by instance status. Counts for pending and terminating instances might be non-zero if the fleet is adjusting to a scaling event or if access to resources is temporarily affected.
---@field Location? aws.gamelift.LocationStringModel The fleet location for the instance count information, expressed as an Amazon Web Services Region code, such as us-west-2.
---@field GameServerContainerGroupCounts? aws.gamelift.GameServerContainerGroupCounts The number and status of game server container groups deployed in a container fleet.
---@field ManagedCapacityConfiguration? aws.gamelift.ManagedCapacityConfiguration Configuration settings for managed capacity scaling.

---@alias aws.gamelift.FleetCapacityList aws.gamelift.FleetCapacity[]

---Describes a container fleet deployment with updates to the fleet.
---@class aws.gamelift.FleetDeployment
---@field DeploymentId? aws.gamelift.DeploymentId A unique identifier for the deployment.
---@field FleetId? aws.gamelift.FleetId A unique identifier for the container fleet.
