---@field GameSessionName? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A descriptive label that is associated with a game session. Session names do not need to be unique.
---@field GameSessionId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString An identifier for the game session that is unique across all regions. The value is always a full ARN in the following format: For Home Region game session - arn:aws:gamelift:::gamesession//. For Remote Location game session - arn:aws:gamelift:::gamesession///. This value is the same as GameSessionArn. This value isn't final until placement status is FULFILLED.
---@field GameSessionArn? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString An identifier for the game session that is unique across all regions. The value is always a full ARN in the following format: For Home Region game session - arn:aws:gamelift:::gamesession//. For Remote Location game session - arn:aws:gamelift:::gamesession///. This value is the same as GameSessionId. This value isn't final until placement status is FULFILLED.
---@field GameSessionRegion? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString Name of the Region where the game session created by this placement request is running. This value isn't final until placement status is FULFILLED.
---@field PlayerLatencies? aws.gamelift.PlayerLatencyList A set of values, expressed in milliseconds, that indicates the amount of latency that a player experiences when connected to a fleet location (Amazon Web Services Regions or custom locations for Amazon GameLift Servers Anywhere fleets).
---@field StartTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp Time stamp indicating when this request was placed in the queue. Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").
---@field EndTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp Time stamp indicating when this request was completed, canceled, or timed out.
---@field IpAddress? distilled.Secret The IP address of the game session. To connect to a Amazon GameLift Servers game server, an app needs both the IP address and port number. This value isn't final until placement status is FULFILLED.
---@field DnsName? aws.gamelift.DnsName The DNS identifier assigned to the instance that is running the game session. Values have the following format:
---@field Port? distilled.Secret The port number for the game session. To connect to a Amazon GameLift Servers game server, an app needs both the IP address and port number. This value isn't final until placement status is FULFILLED.
---@field PlacedPlayerSessions? aws.gamelift.PlacedPlayerSessionList A collection of information on player sessions created in response to the game session placement request. These player sessions are created only after a new game session is successfully placed (placement status is FULFILLED). This information includes the player ID, provided in the placement request, and a corresponding player session ID.
---@field GameSessionData? distilled.Secret A set of custom game session properties, formatted as a single string value. This data is passed to a game server process with a request to start a new game session. For more information, see Start a game session.
---@field MatchmakerData? distilled.Secret Information on the matchmaking process for this game. Data is in JSON syntax, formatted as a string. It identifies the matchmaking configuration used to create the match, and contains data on all players assigned to the match, including player attributes and team assignments. For more details on matchmaker data, see Match Data.
---@field PriorityConfigurationOverride? aws.gamelift.PriorityConfigurationOverride An alternative priority list of locations that's included with a game session placement request. When provided, the list overrides a queue's location order list for this game session placement request only. The list might include Amazon Web Services Regions, local zones, and custom locations (for Anywhere fleets). The fallback strategy tells Amazon GameLift Servers what action to take (if any) in ...
---@field PlayerGatewayStatus? aws.gamelift.PlayerGatewayStatus The current status of player gateway for the game session placement. Note, even if a fleet has PlayerGatewayMode configured as ENABLED, player gateway might not be available in a specific location. For more information about locations where player gateway is supported, see Amazon GameLift Servers service locations.

---@alias aws.gamelift.GameSessionPlacementState "PENDING"|"FULFILLED"|"CANCELLED"|"TIMED_OUT"|"FAILED"

---Configuration for a game session placement mechanism that processes requests for new game sessions. A queue can be used on its own or as part of a matchmaking solution.
---@class aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueue
---@field Name? aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueName A descriptive label that is associated with game session queue. Queue names must be unique within each Region.
---@field GameSessionQueueArn? aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is assigned to a Amazon GameLift Servers game session queue resource and uniquely identifies it. ARNs are unique across all Regions. Format is arn:aws:gamelift:::gamesessionqueue/. In a Amazon GameLift Servers game session queue ARN, the resource ID matches the Name value.
---@field TimeoutInSeconds? aws.gamelift.WholeNumber The maximum time, in seconds, that a new game session placement request remains in the queue. When a request exceeds this time, the game session placement changes to a TIMED_OUT status.
---@field PlayerLatencyPolicies? aws.gamelift.PlayerLatencyPolicyList A set of policies that enforce a sliding cap on player latency when processing game sessions placement requests. Use multiple policies to gradually relax the cap over time if Amazon GameLift Servers can't make a placement. Policies are evaluated in order starting with the lowest maximum latency value.
---@field Destinations? aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueDestinationList A list of fleets and/or fleet aliases that can be used to fulfill game session placement requests in the queue. Destinations are identified by either a fleet ARN or a fleet alias ARN, and are listed in order of placement preference.
---@field FilterConfiguration? aws.gamelift.FilterConfiguration A list of locations where a queue is allowed to place new game sessions. Locations are specified in the form of Amazon Web Services Region codes, such as us-west-2. If this parameter is not set, game sessions can be placed in any queue location.
---@field PriorityConfiguration? aws.gamelift.PriorityConfiguration Custom settings to use when prioritizing destinations and locations for game session placements. This configuration replaces the default prioritization process. Priority types that are not explicitly named will be automatically applied at the end of the prioritization process.
---@field CustomEventData? distilled.Secret Information that is added to all events that are related to this game session queue.
---@field NotificationTarget? aws.gamelift.QueueSnsArnStringModel An SNS topic ARN that is set up to receive game session placement notifications. See Setting up notifications for game session placement.
---@field LogConfiguration? aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueLogConfiguration An optional configuration that delivers game session placement insight logs to one or more destinations of your choice. Use these logs to diagnose why a game session placement is FULFILLED, CANCELLED, TIMED_OUT, or FAILED, which locations were evaluated, and the latency and cost factors that influenced each decision.

---@alias aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueArn string

---A fleet or alias designated in a game session queue. Queues fulfill requests for new game sessions by placing a new game session on any of the queue's destinations.
---@class aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueDestination
---@field DestinationArn? aws.gamelift.ArnStringModel The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is assigned to fleet or fleet alias. ARNs, which include a fleet ID or alias ID and a Region name, provide a unique identifier across all Regions.

---@alias aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueDestinationList aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueDestination[]

---@alias aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueList aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueue[]

---A configuration that delivers game session placement insight logs to one or more destinations of your choice.
---@class aws.gamelift.GameSessionQueueLogConfiguration
---@field DeliveryDestinations aws.gamelift.LogDeliveryDestinationList The destinations that receive game session placement insight logs for the queue. You can specify up to 3 destinations. Each destination must have a unique ARN.

