---Describes a support container in a container group. A support container might be in a game server container group or a per-instance container group. Support containers don't run game server processes.
---@class aws.gamelift.SupportContainerDefinition
---@field ContainerName? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAnd128MaxAsciiString The container definition identifier. Container names are unique within a container group definition.
---@field DependsOn? aws.gamelift.ContainerDependencyList Indicates that the container relies on the status of other containers in the same container group during its startup and shutdown sequences. A container might have dependencies on multiple containers.
---@field MountPoints? aws.gamelift.ContainerMountPointList A mount point that binds a path inside the container to a file or directory on the host system and lets it access the file or directory.
---@field EnvironmentOverride? aws.gamelift.ContainerEnvironmentList A set of environment variables that's passed to the container on startup. See the ContainerDefinition::environment parameter in the Amazon Elastic Container Service API Reference.
---@field Essential? aws.gamelift.BooleanModel Indicates whether the container is vital to the container group. If an essential container fails, the entire container group restarts.
---@field HealthCheck? aws.gamelift.ContainerHealthCheck A configuration for a non-terminal health check. A support container automatically restarts if it stops functioning or if it fails this health check.
---@field ImageUri? aws.gamelift.ImageUriString The URI to the image that Amazon GameLift Servers deploys to a container fleet. For a more specific identifier, see ResolvedImageDigest.
---@field MemoryHardLimitMebibytes? aws.gamelift.ContainerMemoryLimit The amount of memory that Amazon GameLift Servers makes available to the container. If memory limits aren't set for an individual container, the container shares the container group's total memory allocation.
---@field PortConfiguration? aws.gamelift.ContainerPortConfiguration A set of ports that allow access to the container from external users. Processes running in the container can bind to one of these ports. Container ports aren't directly accessed by inbound traffic. Amazon GameLift Servers maps these container ports to externally accessible connection ports, which are assigned as needed from the container fleet's ConnectionPortRange.
---@field ResolvedImageDigest? aws.gamelift.Sha256 A unique and immutable identifier for the container image. The digest is a SHA 256 hash of the container image manifest.
---@field Vcpu? aws.gamelift.ContainerVcpu The number of vCPU units that are reserved for the container. If no resources are reserved, the container shares the total vCPU limit for the container group.
---@field LinuxCapabilities? aws.gamelift.LinuxCapabilities Linux-specific modifications that are applied to the default Docker container configuration, such as Linux capabilities. For more information see LinuxCapabilities.

---Describes a support container in a container group. You can define a support container in either a game server container group or a per-instance container group. Support containers don't run game server processes.
---@class aws.gamelift.SupportContainerDefinitionInput
---@field ContainerName aws.gamelift.NonZeroAnd128MaxAsciiString A string that uniquely identifies the container definition within a container group.
