---Represents an authorization for a VPC peering connection between the VPC for an Amazon GameLift Servers fleet and another VPC on an account you have access to. This authorization must exist and be valid for the peering connection to be established. Authorizations are valid for 24 hours after they are issued.
---@class aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringAuthorization
---@field GameLiftAwsAccountId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for the Amazon Web Services account that you use to manage your Amazon GameLift Servers fleet. You can find your Account ID in the Amazon Web Services Management Console under account settings.
---@field PeerVpcAwsAccountId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString The authorization's peer VPC Amazon Web Services account ID.
---@field PeerVpcId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for a VPC with resources to be accessed by your Amazon GameLift Servers fleet. The VPC must be in the same Region as your fleet. To look up a VPC ID, use the VPC Dashboard in the Amazon Web Services Management Console. Learn more about VPC peering in VPC Peering with Amazon GameLift Servers Fleets.
---@field CreationTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp Time stamp indicating when this authorization was issued. Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").
---@field ExpirationTime? aws.gamelift.Timestamp Time stamp indicating when this authorization expires (24 hours after issuance). Format is a number expressed in Unix time as milliseconds (for example "1469498468.057").

---@alias aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringAuthorizationList aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringAuthorization[]

---Represents a peering connection between a VPC on one of your Amazon Web Services accounts and the VPC for your Amazon GameLift Servers fleets. This record may be for an active peering connection or a pending connection that has not yet been established.
---@class aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringConnection
---@field FleetId? aws.gamelift.FleetId A unique identifier for the fleet. This ID determines the ID of the Amazon GameLift Servers VPC for your fleet.
---@field FleetArn? aws.gamelift.FleetArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) associated with the GameLift fleet resource for this connection.
---@field IpV4CidrBlock? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString CIDR block of IPv4 addresses assigned to the VPC peering connection for the GameLift VPC. The peered VPC also has an IPv4 CIDR block associated with it; these blocks cannot overlap or the peering connection cannot be created.
---@field VpcPeeringConnectionId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier that is automatically assigned to the connection record. This ID is referenced in VPC peering connection events, and is used when deleting a connection.
---@field Status? aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringConnectionStatus The status information about the connection. Status indicates if a connection is pending, successful, or failed.
---@field PeerVpcId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for a VPC with resources to be accessed by your Amazon GameLift Servers fleet. The VPC must be in the same Region as your fleet. To look up a VPC ID, use the VPC Dashboard in the Amazon Web Services Management Console. Learn more about VPC peering in VPC Peering with Amazon GameLift Servers Fleets.
---@field GameLiftVpcId? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString A unique identifier for the VPC that contains the Amazon GameLift Servers fleet for this connection. This VPC is managed by Amazon GameLift Servers and does not appear in your Amazon Web Services account.

---@alias aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringConnectionList aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringConnection[]

---Represents status information for a VPC peering connection. Status codes and messages are provided from EC2 (see VpcPeeringConnectionStateReason). Connection status information is also communicated as a fleet event.
---@class aws.gamelift.VpcPeeringConnectionStatus
---@field Code? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString Code indicating the status of a VPC peering connection.
---@field Message? aws.gamelift.NonZeroAndMaxString Additional messaging associated with the connection status.

